course: dictionary
lesson: 3245
title: Epic: stories, journeys and slang
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Epic» can be a noun or an adjective. As a noun it means a long poem or story about heroes and their adventures, such as the Epic of Gilgamesh. As an adjective it means very big, long, brave or impressive, like «an epic journey».
explain: Use the context to choose the meaning. The sentence «The Epic of Gilgamesh is one of the oldest stories ever written down» is about a story, so epic is a noun here. The sentence «an epic battle» describes something big and exciting, so epic is an adjective.
explain: Slang changes the meaning again. «That party was epic!» means it was really great, and «an epic fail» means a huge, funny failure. Ask yourself: is the word naming a story, or describing something big or amazing?
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. «The Epic of Gilgamesh is one of the oldest stories» still makes sense with the meaning long story, so the noun meaning fits. Your check tells you which meaning to pick.
fact: Epic is a noun and an adjective.
fact: «The Epic of Gilgamesh» is an ancient story from Mesopotamia about a king named Gilgamesh.
fact: In the Epic of Gilgamesh, a king loses his best friend Enkidu and learns that all people die.
fact: As an adjective, «epic» means very big, long, brave or impressive, as in «an epic journey».
fact: In slang, «epic» can mean really great, as in «That party was epic!»
exercise: «The Epic of Gilgamesh is one of the oldest stories ever written down.» In this sentence, what is an epic? | A small pet | A type of mud brick | A kind of petrol | *A long story about heroes and adventures
exercise: «an epic journey» What does epic mean here? | Very short and quiet | Written in clay | Lost or missing | *Very big, long and impressive
exercise: «That party was epic!» What does epic mean? | A stepped tower | A huge failure | *Really great and amazing | Boring and slow
test: Why can we still read the Epic of Gilgamesh today? | The king read it aloud to everyone in the city | Stories were always printed in gold | The story was painted on the walls of a school | *Baked clay does not rot or burn away easily, so many clay tablets survive
test: In «an epic battle», which meaning of epic fits best? | A slang word for silly | *Big, huge and exciting | A story written in clay | A stepped tower of mud brick
exam: Which sentence uses epic as a noun? | «That party was epic!» | «We had an epic fail and laughed.» | *«The Epic of Gilgamesh is one of the oldest stories ever written down.» | «The journey was epic and very long.»
